course: dictionary
lesson: 10950
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Waiter is one of them. Most of the time it means a person who brings food and drinks in a restaurant or café. Rarely, it means someone who waits.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. Read the words around it: «In a restaurant you speak quietly, stay in your seat and are polite to the waiter.» Restaurant and seat are your clues, so the waiter is the person who serves you.
explain: Check by putting your meaning into the sentence. Does "the person who brings food and drinks" fit? Yes, it does, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A waiter is a person whose job is to bring food and drinks to people in a restaurant or café.
fact: Rarely, a waiter is someone who waits. This meaning is not the one you will meet most often.
fact: Useful phrases: «ask the waiter», «waiter, please», «the waiter brought».
fact: In the USA, tips are part of a waiter's pay, so people often leave about 15 to 20 percent of the bill.
fact: In France, «S'il vous plaît!» with a small raised hand is a polite way to call a waiter. Shouting «garçon» is old-fashioned and rude today.
exercise: «The waiter brought our soup, still hot.» What does a waiter do? | *Brings food and drinks to people in a restaurant | Cooks food in a kitchen at home | Sings songs for the guests | Sells tickets at the door
exercise: «In a restaurant you speak quietly, stay in your seat and are polite to the waiter.» How should you act towards the waiter? | Shout across the room | Climb on the table | Leave without paying | *Be polite
exercise: In France, which is a polite way to call a waiter? | *Saying «S'il vous plaît!» with a small raised hand | Shouting «garçon» across the café | Throwing a napkin | Banging the table with a spoon
test: «Please wait for the waiter to bring the bill.» Which meaning is used here? | *The person who brings food and drinks in a restaurant | A chair in the room | A kind of coat | Someone who is patient and calm
test: Which clue in «In a restaurant you speak quietly, stay in your seat and are polite to the waiter.» helps you find the meaning of waiter? | *The word restaurant | The word polite | The word stay alone | The word quietly
exam: Which sentence uses waiter with its common meaning? | The waiter climbed the tall tree. | The waiter sang a song on the stage. | The waiter ran in the park all morning. | *«The waiter brought our drinks.»
